# Frontend and design constraints
- Read `docs/DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md` and relevant parts of `PROJECT_SPEC.md` before implementing UI. Compare Map-tab changes against `references/map-tab-reference.png`.
- Keep the map as the dominant canvas. Preserve the floating reward header, destination search, category chips, illustrated/pastel geographic basemap, custom fox marker, colored dotted routes, place popups, floating route/list controls, and fixed five-tab navigation.
- Use theme tokens and reusable React/TypeScript components. Anchor color: Kyoto Purple `#782459`; warm cream and pale yellow accents; avoid an overly pink, generic SaaS look.
- The real basemap must remain pannable and zoomable. Do not use the reference screenshot as a fake map background.
- Use replaceable placeholders for original fox/icon artwork until assets are supplied. Do not generate substitute branded characters.
- Support English and Japanese through localization keys; do not hardcode English-only UI in components. Respect touch targets, safe-area insets, contrast, and reduced-motion preferences.
- No dead controls: anything visible must respond or be explicitly marked as nonfunctional preview.
